  "step_3": "The decision reason requires computing differences between outcomes and a reference value (set to -3000 due to B’s sure outcome), then evaluating the mean of those differences weighted by probabilities. The individual does not mention the reference value, nor do they compute or reference any differences from a baseline. Instead, their justification is based on avoiding a certain loss and valuing the possibility of zero loss. This is a different type of reasoning—focused on risk aversion and the presence of a non-loss outcome—rather than on mean differences from a reference. Therefore, the individual did not apply the specified decision reason. The information considered (presence of a zero-loss possibility vs. certain loss) differs from the required elements (differences from reference value and mean difference calculation). The justification also does not follow the rule of preferring the lottery with the more favorable mean difference. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

